<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell nine points to 1,450.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell nine points to 1,450.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,450 today from 1,459 on April 4, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.  Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1467    13.319	  1475    13.394</p>
<p>   1a   1461 11069.000	  1469 11125.000</p>
<p>   2    1741    24.875	  1760    25.138</p>
<p>   2a   1796 14731.000	  1805 14806.000</p>
<p>   3    1681    15.506	  1700    15.688</p>
<p>   3a   1510 11919.000	  1526 12044.000</p>
<p>   6    1233    12.719	  1234    12.731</p>
